__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
build/
dist/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# The tests generate a CA, a server certificate and a server key into pytest's tmp dir every
# session, and the anchor manifest they write is derived from them. None of it is evidence: a
# committed throwaway key would look like a pin, and a pin is exactly the thing this repository
# must never gain by accident.
#
# `tests/fixtures/*` rather than `tests/fixtures/` so the two files below can be re-included: they
# are not generated output but captured evidence - the real keys and real STHs of two production
# logs, which the pinning tests need in order to refuse a fake rather than only another fake.
tests/fixtures/*
!tests/fixtures/log-pins.toml
!tests/fixtures/production-sth.json
